  "rule_description": "JEP 390 (JDK 16) designated the primitive wrapper classes as value-based and deprecated their constructors for removal. Compiling JADE on JDK 17 with -Xlint:removal produces 144 removal warnings for new Boolean/Integer/Long/Double/Float/Character calls -- the single largest terminally-deprecated surface in the codebase. The code still compiles and runs on 17; the exposure is that these constructors are the ones scheduled to disappear. The fix is the documented replacement, the corresponding valueOf factory.",
